@aiwayds/dsh-web-search-anysearch README · Install：> `@deepseek-ai/*` packages are **peer dependencies by design**: they must resolve to
> the profile's single shared dsh closure. Putting them in `dependencies` installs a
> second cordis instance and crashes the loader.

@aiwayds/dsh-web-search-anysearch README · Uninstall：There is no on-disk state to clean up: the plugin is stateless (no cache, no
config writes). The optional API key, if you ever stored one, lives in the
host-owned credentials document — remove it there if unwanted.

@aiwayds/dsh-web-search-anysearch README · Develop：```sh
npm install
npm run check   # tsc --noEmit
npm test        # build + node --test (transport runs against a local HTTP server;
                #  markdown fixtures come from real API payloads)

After editing `src/`, run `npm run build` and restart dsh.
